  "query_preview": "..\n\nSYNOPTIC SETUP:\n\nA low pressure system over Idaho this morning is tracking east \nacross southern Montana and northern Wyoming for the rest of today \nand tomorrow. This system is cutoff by a northern stream shallow \nridge in the Canadian Prairies which is leading to dry air cutting\noff areas north of a line from Malta to Medicine Lake. There has\nalready been over an inch of rain in southern Garfield County.\nThis will in our awareness through tomorrow. There may even be an\nextension to the Flood Advisory that is in effect there. Up to an \nadditional half inch of rain is expected for southern Garfield \nCounty. This includes Prairie, Dawson, Wibaux, and the southern\nhalf of Richland county through noon Sunday before the system\nmoves east. \n\nA moderately strong ridge is expected to move in on Monday, and\ntemperatures are expected to rebound above average from Tuesday\nthrough Friday. There may be a shortwave trough across the\nsoutheast to bring a slight chance of precipitation on Wednesday\nevening though.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nThe only deviation was to increase winds at high elevation\nlocations through tomorrow.\n\nThere is moderate to high confidence in rainfall amounts through\ntomorrow evening.\n\nThere is high confidence of an upper ridge moving in on Monday,\nand low confidence on accumulating precipitation moving in on \nWednesday evening.",
